      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly. Review your website's and any third-party apps' security measures for potential weaknesses like weak passwords, outdated software, or unencrypted data transmissions, all of which can increase vulnerability. Audit your systems regularly to identify and fix security gaps. Also, consider encryption for secure transactions and opt-in for secure Data Protection Impact Assessments to preemptively evaluate potential risks. Furthermore, be cautious of social engineering tactics that could trick employees into giving away sensitive information inadvertently. Regular staff training can help safeguard against these \"sneaky\" risks.",
