      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Indeed, sophisticated attackers often use automated bots to conduct a range of malicious activities, including phishing, credential stuffing, and brute force attacks, to gain unauthorized access to systems.\n\nTo protect against these \"hidden\" intrusions, implement strong, unique passwords with multi-factor authentication for system access. Keep software up to date to defend against known vulnerabilities and employ web application firewalls (WAFs) to block malicious traffic. Conduct regular penetration testing to probe for weaknesses that automated bots or skilled hackers might find. Additionally, monitoring and alerting systems can notify you immediately of suspicious activities, allowing you to respond swiftly to any \"under the radar\" intrusions.",
      "source": "target",
